# Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's target
# directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the published folder
# is published. That is what Mod/ is for: the junction from RimWorld/Mods points there, and
# everything else in this repository - Art/, scripts/, this file - stays out of reach by
# construction.

# Build intermediates.
# Source/Directory.Build.props sends them to build/, outside Mod/: they
# must never end up inside it, since Mod/ goes to the Workshop as it stands.
build/
Source/**/obj/
Source/**/bin/

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings. Until this folder became a repository of its
# own the rule lived in the monorepo's .gitignore, a file this repository does not carry.
.claude/

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# RimWorld converts every PNG to a .dds next to it the first time the game loads the mod. They are
# a per-machine cache, regenerated on demand. The Steam remark at the top of this file applies:
# ignoring them here does not keep them out of a folder uploaded straight from disk.
*.dds

# Pickle's -EvidenceDir target. Proof kept on disk for the session that reads it, not something the
# repository carries: screenshots and Player.log make it grow without bound (PickleTools saw 10 GB
# in a day). What is worth keeping goes to docs/runs/ as a short text summary.
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/

# Images from test runs. docs/runs/ holds text summaries only; a capture that proves something is
# described in words there, and the file itself stays on disk under Tests/Pickle/Evidence/.
docs/runs/*.png
docs/runs/*.gif

# Preview renderer QA output (PUBLISHING.md, "Jeu minimal de sources et sorties de Preview").
Art/.render/
